{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538506754,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEzNjEzMjM2Nw=="},"target":"bea9a9d384a8ea2756d40f1086afcd54a869a1af7cf69c312d184162bf425de3","message":"This discussion would not be new, previous ones:\n- #378 (Brainstorming for \"git annex unlock\" use) - boiled down to use unlock/lock pair\n- #453 (initial title is irrelevant) - has [joey's comment](https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220850060) on `git annex adjust --unlock`\n\nI still think that in particular with Python API it would be a big convenience to the users to be able to manipulate file content in basic operations without doing all the manual get/unlock/lock/... combination.  E.g.  something like\n\n## 'w' mode:\n\n```python\nwith ds.open(\"filename\", \"w\") as f:\n   f.write(\"new content replacing the old one even if it was not present\")\n```\nwhich would do \n- `rm filename`\n- `open(\"filename\", \"w\")`\n- ... (context) \n- `git annex add \"filename\"`\n\n## \"a\" (`b` or not)\n\nit would \n- `get`\n- `unlock`\n- `open(\"filename\", \"a\")`;\n- ...\n- `git annex add ...`\n\n## 'r'\n\n- `get`\n- `open`\n\nin `w` and `a` mode if possible/needing hiding any v5 vs v6 peculiarities (i.e. locking it back so real symlink is committed and not git reference file).\n\nedit 1:  for files under git, should be regular `open; git add`\n\nWhat do you think?","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538506713,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE4ODAxNjE3ODA="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538506713,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE4ODAxNjE3ODE="},"added":["UX"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1538509147,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjQwMzQ5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2890#issuecomment-426403496"},"message":"Cool!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1538516393,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjQzOTk5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2890#issuecomment-426439992"},"message":"Nice.\n\n\u003e in w and a mode if possible/needing hiding any v5 vs v6 peculiarities (i.e. locking it back so real symlink is committed and not git reference file).\n\nThe `git annex add` in your steps above will do that.  If the file was already unlocked, should it remain unlocked?\n\n\u003e edit 1: for files under git, should be regular open; git add\n\nI wonder if it'd be worth having this at the level of `datalad.api`.  If `datalad.api.open` was used outside of a repo, it could collapse entirely to the built-in `open`, which may be handy for giving someone a script that works without the entire dataset.  Not sure.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538516673,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjQ0MTE5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2890#issuecomment-426441193"},"message":"Re API level: I had similar thoughts... probably should be implemented as such just with `@datasetmethod` as the other similar api \"methods\" we have","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538516746,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjQ0MTQ4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2890#issuecomment-426441482"},"message":"Re unlocked state... without all the revolution - do we have a method already to give this status?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1538517320,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjQ0MzkxMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2890#issuecomment-426443910"},"message":"\u003e Re unlocked state... without all the revolution - do we have a method already to give this status?\n\nNot that I'm aware of.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538528005,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjQ3ODAyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2890#issuecomment-426478028"},"message":"having thought about the locked/unlocked: it should probably just rely on what `datalad add` does, and also pass into it `save/--nosave` argument, so we decide just in one place what is happening to unlocked files.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1538561363,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjU4MTA1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2890#issuecomment-426581058"},"message":"Well, but if that magic `open` is going to unlock a file, `datalad add` would always find an unlocked file later on. So, it can't be the only place to deal with that. `open` needs know whether it found the file unlocked initially and if not so, lock it again in v6 before saving.","files":null}]}